{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/938071-several-rules-questions-humanity-defence-to-disciplines-defending-others-safe-house","id":938071,"title":"Several rules questions - Humanity,defence to disciplines,defending others,safe house","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-27T06:42:07-07:00","id":938071,"title":"Several rules questions - Humanity,defence to disciplines,defending others,safe house","content":"Hello, me and my best friend are starting a vampire game he is going to GM it and I will assist when needed as we have a large group of 8 players and there are several rules that we are debating about. We both have characters that will be involved in the game.<br /> <br /> 1 - Humanity breaking point - We are trying to work out where self defence killing would go on breaking points, we see at 4 is accident 3 passioned 2 premediated. He is saying it is 2 because you kill someone on purpose I am saying lowest 5. View points being 4 is accident which could be your negligence such as speeding in a car and killing someone. Self defence killing is this guy just stabbed someone and is coming at me with a knife I hit him with my sword and he died. Or theres this guy about to kill an innocent person/group so I shoot him to stop him he dies from it. My friend thinks that because you are chosing to kill them its a 2 breaking point you could just ignore it and walk away.<br /> <br /> 2 - Defence to disciplines - He is saying to get around dominate his character is just never going to look anyone in the eye, I said that is stupidly cheap and if you have an audience with the prince/sheriff and refuse to look them in the eye you'll end up having no eyes. He said no every vampire will do it as a norm to protect against dominate even the prince will do it. Is it really that easy to just negate a whole discipline? Just say to the GM just so you know my character never looks anyone in the eye? I'll walk around with headphones in and never looking anyone in the eye and I negate dominate and majesty with no effort or xp on my part.<br /> <br /> 3 - Defending for others - No rules for this but if I made a bodyguard or had one, how would it go them defending for someone? I was thinking they would need to go first and withold their action and then use it when someone attacks the person they are protecting to get in the way? But you act do your attack/move then they could just side step around you and hit the person your protecting as they act after you? Any rules for this anywhere?<br /> <br /> 4 - Lastly safe house - We were wondering it is very non descript about what you can have and how to get around it etc, so can you just say you have 20 dogs 5 traps 12 security guards 17 sensors 30 cameras etc? Only asking as my friend said that if you do some research and hack the cameras and chuck some drugged meat over the walls for the dogs to eat you can lower the defence rating the safe house gives you. So if you can through just mundane means lower the security a safe house provides how do you govern how much stuff is in your safe house? Also he said you can have loads of fire traps so it does 5 aggravated to vampires trying to break in, as the merit says you can have traps that deal lethal damage equal to its safe house rating so he said chose a fire trap then it does 5 agg. I think this again is bending what was intended but we decided to have it run like that but just wanted peoples thoughts.<br /> <br /> Sorry long rants but needed to clear these up and explain view points, any thoughts would be great thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:52:44-07:00","id":938109,"title":"","content":"1: I would put self defense at 7 if there truly was NO other way or perhaps an accident as you were defending. But that moment where they have knocked out the bad guy and could have walked away, but kept swinging... that is no longer self defense but a choice. I some what agree with your friend. If you a trained with something and you know you are going to kill them and not disable them, and you do it anyway... It's 3 impassioned ( premeditated is when you plan it and seek it. ) So you really have to watch the fine lines there. For example. If you are a black belt and you get into a bar fight and kill someone. you get into way way worse trouble than if you were drunk john doe. <br /> <br /> 2: There is a HUGE thread about dominate and not looking into eyes. I Suppose it is possible to blind yourself in some way before hand, but in the real world if you're in a fight, you use your eyes for a lot more than one might think they do. So, the consensus ( unless I am wrong on that ) was no, you cant just not look. Also Majesty doesn't need eye contact... It's more that feeling you just know they are there, aware of their presence. ( like the first dot, awe, they dont need to see or hear you even across a crowded room, and yet they know you want them to come over )<br /> <br /> 3: Good question. I know there is a human sheild rule, but that's if you are holding them to protect you... I am not aware of anything else, but It would be a neat fighting style to make ( if something doesnt already exist ) where perhaps you can spend a will power to force some one to attack you instead, like goad in DND <br /> <br /> 4: No it would be lethal. So clearly, it cant be something like that for free and since it says lethal, it would get downgraded to bashing for Vampires. Perhaps you could purchase and &quot;advanced&quot; safe house ( homebrew territory ) to make your traps deal aggravated damage. Also you dont lower the defense for drugging and hacking. I would perhaps give them a plus for &quot;equipment&quot; on rolling to break in. Say they have 6 dice to break in + 3 for equipment ( drugging and hacking ) - 5 for the dots in safe house. = 4 dice to break in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:45:07-07:00","id":938140,"title":"","content":"1. I'd say to just forget if it was in self-defense or not. I think that's meaningless - Humanity is supposed to measure how much empathy you have for your fellow humans. It is not a measurement of your morality. So, while self-defense is a strong <i>moral and legal argument</i>, it has no relationship to how a person relates to humans. If you bust out the Claws of the Unholy everytime you're attacked, that's showing a callous attitude towards life, even if its only done in self defense. Meanwhile, someone that perfects choke holds or use of stun guns to immobilize attackers in such a way that no one ends up seriously hurt? They're much more careful with life.<br /> <br /> 2. This is nothing more than trying to be a munchkin. And there are plenty of tricks to catch someone's eye and draw their attention, even without magic. I'd just tell the player &quot;No&quot; and be done with it - I think of this as an OOC player attempt to game the system, so I think that it should be adressed in the same way. Alternatively, if you prefer an IC method, they get a Blind Condition when related to perception of other people as well as a social penalty for being so obvious. <br /> <br /> 3. I personally treat a bodyguard as Cover, making it hard to reach or hit the protected person, as well as reducing the potency of all attacks. I may switch things up depending on the situation. As well, there's actually a pretty cool Temple Guardian FS in the Secrets of the Covenant CotC preview that works as a bodyguard for others. I highly recommend checking it out.<br /> <br /> 4. Nope. IC descriptions are justifications for purchasing the regular merits, not getting free merits. Descriptions on how you're breaking in don't modify someone else's merits, but provide you equipment bonuses to your rolls. You want to deal aggravated damage, then, like Vitalis said, you could come up with a new merit that deals that kind of damage. Though, for the record, I wouldn't allow it with the justifiaction &quot;Its fire!&quot; Ghouls and hellhounds don't suffer agg from flame, after all, so this is a bit questionable, as well as the fact there's Resilience or armor or other damage reducing measures that would apply. And I would suggest kindly that any vampire installing fire into their home is rather suicidal, since if someone breaks into the home in the middle of the day (most home robberies happen during that time, when people are usually away from home at work) and lights the place on fire, you've basically set your own haven on fire with you sleeping inside. Death trap anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:07:36-07:00","id":938159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/938071-several-rules-questions-humanity-defence-to-disciplines-defending-others-safe-house?p=938140#post938140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I'd say to just forget if it was in self-defense or not. I think that's meaningless - Humanity is supposed to measure how much empathy you have for your fellow humans. It is not a measurement of your morality. So, while self-defense is a strong <i>moral and legal argument</i>, it has no relationship to how a person relates to humans. If you bust out the Claws of the Unholy everytime you're attacked, that's showing a callous attitude towards life, even if its only done in self defense. Meanwhile, someone that perfects choke holds or use of stun guns to immobilize attackers in such a way that no one ends up seriously hurt? They're much more careful with life.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with you completely there, I think he is asking how to deal with it Mechanically. As rolling 1 or 5 dice can be the difference of passing the check or not. what would you make the check if it was truly a self-defense act with no other way ( or self defense and an accident ) <br /> <br /> Accident like: you were shooting the bad guy because he kept stabbing you. You got 3 3 then 8 successes and they bled out because you failed the medicine check to keep them alive. Sure you might feel like shit, but how many dice are you rolling? ( lots of people have guns for self defense, which is why I picked this one )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:39:26-07:00","id":938173,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, I would just ignore the fact it was self defense. No bonus dice, no changing the level, nothing. I don't think that self defense applies in this situation, and should have absolutely no mechanical impact.<br /> <br /> Shooting someone because they kept stabbing you is, honestly, something I would qualify as either impassioned (you panicked) or a deliberate murder. Being stabbed is just bashing to a vampire. Pulling out a Predator's Aura, some grappling with a physical, or anything other power else could easily solve a fight against a mortal with zero casualties. You chose to go for a deadly weapon against a mortal in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:44:57-07:00","id":938176,"title":"","content":"I run self defense as a +1 to +3 dice modifier to checks based on the circumstances. You kill someone who attacks you first. Impassioned killing. You provoke someone into taking a swing so you can hit back. (Either by verbal insults or vandalism of their property etc.) Premeditated.<br /> <br /> Gaming the eye contact wording. Nope. Doesn't fly with me unless your character is blind, which includes an inability to use Auspex and permanent penalties. If you're going to stare at the floor the entire time you get perception and combat penalties and the Dominate user still only takes a -2 to mesmerize you because their power oozes from their voice and body language as well.<br /> <br /> Bodyguards I have function as cover, armor, bonus to surprise checks etc. Depending on the circumstance.<br /> <br /> As noted by others, drugging the dogs counts as a one shot situational bonus to break in. You throw poisoned meat over the fence? Maybe the dog is trained to only eat food from their handler. I know some military and police dogs are trained like that.<br /> Firetraps would do aggravated damage to vampires. But it's kind of stupid for a vampire to sleep in a firetrap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-27-2016, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:51:06-07:00","id":938180,"title":"","content":"On the humanity point as 2 is premeditated your saying that someone who thinks you know what I'm going to kill this pregnant woman because she won't give me her purse is the same as there's a murderer he just killed one person he's about to stab a child he is bringing down the knife you have a second to react so as you have a gun in hand you shoot him it is a lucky shot (lots of open rolls) and manages to kill him is the same? I tell you I would feel a lot worse killing a pregnant woman to get her purse than shooting a murderer who was about to kill a child because I had no other choice. I would still feel bad I killed him but would seek solace in the fact I had no choice and he was about to kill a child.<br /> <br /> Thanks suggestions have been helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:45:38-07:00","id":938202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBoyDante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/938071-several-rules-questions-humanity-defence-to-disciplines-defending-others-safe-house?p=938180#post938180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the humanity point as 2 is premeditated your saying that someone who thinks you know what I'm going to kill this pregnant woman because she won't give me her purse is the same as there's a murderer he just killed one person he's about to stab a child he is bringing down the knife you have a second to react so as you have a gun in hand you shoot him it is a lucky shot (lots of open rolls) and manages to kill him is the same? I tell you I would feel a lot worse killing a pregnant woman to get her purse than shooting a murderer who was about to kill a child because I had no other choice. I would still feel bad I killed him but would seek solace in the fact I had no choice and he was about to kill a child.</div> </div> </div> </div> First of all? Split second decisions are not premeditation. That's textbook impassioned killing / manslaughter. The very basis of your argument is already questionable since we're talking two different levels of humanity.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you're equating morality with humanity here. This has nothing to do how good it makes you feel. It has everything to do with how well you relate to people. You're making a cold blooded decision that some lives are worth less than others. That not all human life has value worth keeping. Make no mistake - you can be a very moral person and have low Humanity as well as maintain a high Humanity while being a rather immoral person. There's absolutely nothing wrong with coming to the conclusion that you're an avenging monster that punishes killers and protects the innocent - that's a major philosphy within the Lancea et Sanctum. It may be a very inhuman way of thinking, but I'd say its a rather positive outlook.<br /> <br /> Third, Dominate can just easily stop a killer in this situation, as can Celerity, Nightmare, using Vigor to throw an object, and any number of other powers. Using a gun in this case is still choosing a lethal option over several readily available non-lethal alternatives that are just as fast and likely more effective. Shooting someone doesn't neceesarily stop or put them down, but using Celerity to impose yourself between a knife and victim is absolutely going to work. This situation is nothing more than an reducive scenario, trying to give a binary solution when there's a bunch of potential options at your finger tips, including getting involved before the situations devolves to this point. <i>Reduct ad absurdum </i> is a logical fallacy for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:05:43-07:00","id":938217,"title":"","content":"1. Killing (or doing anything else) in self defense isn't a breaking point by itself. Depending on the nature of the killing, I'd say it's a Humanity 1 or Humanity 2 breaking point. If you want how guilty a character feels to figure into it, shift it up or down a level. Keep in mind, though, that the struggle against detachment based on mitigating factors is what the roll is already meant to measure.<br /> <br /> 2. Attempts to avoid eye contact are already part of the dice pool to resist Mesmerize.<br /> <br /> 3. I'd let the bodyguard add one Attribute or Skill to the defended character's Defense. Depending on the context, this might be Stamina (I'm protecting you with the sheer bulk of my body), Weaponry (I'm blocking attacks on you using a tool or weapon), Dexterity (I jump between you and your attacker with lightning speed), or even Resolve (I resist my fear of fire to stand between you and the torch-wielding hunter).<br /> <br /> If that pushes Defense too high for your taste, consider something like substituting the bodyguard's appropriate stat for the defended character's Athletics in calculating Defense.<br /> <br /> A character should not be able to benefit from a bodyguard physically blocking attacks while also making attacks themselves. Unless maybe they have a cool new description for how they do it, in which case go to town. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 4. Safe Place is primarily meant for player characters. If you're attempting to lay siege to a non-player character's home or bolt-hole, and want to cover it in detail, you're better off designing it by statting traps and opposing characters individually. When player characters are being attacked in their own Safe Place, follow the damage guidelines on p. 123. If a character wants to buy security, consider making a Retainer, using Resources to get equipment/services like Surveillance (p. 189), Bodyguard Service, or Security Consulting (both on p. 185).<br /> <br /> If you want to get deep into building your own security measures (animate or not), try the Building Equipment rules from the <i>Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:06:00-07:00","id":938218,"title":"","content":"The premise of the argument is you have no other choice, your too far away to run Inbetween, no thrown weapons near by, tried to shout but he ignored you, only have celerity and already used your vitae this turn only have a gun in hand and if you don't act now he will be stabbed. You aim for the arm to get him to stop but it severs an artery and he bleeds out.<br /> <br /> And it's about if that is a low breaking point I wouldn't see it personally as a low breaking point for my humanity I would be praised a hero and feel good that I saved someone. Humanity wise it may still haunt me but I don't think it should be a 2 breaking point is what I'm saying. I think it should be lowest 4 but would place it at 5 self defence with no other option still bad but not as bad as premeditated/passioned killing which we see as crimes of passion like you come home your wife's cheating and you snap and kill her. I still see it as a breaking point but just don't think it should be on the same level as premeditated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:17:25-07:00","id":938225,"title":"","content":"If it helps, the breaking points listed in the book are meant to be &quot;examples only&quot; (p.107) and customized for your game or shifted up and down to fit the situation. My answer's from the perspective of the sample breaking point chart, but you can adjust it if you feel the moral component is an important factor in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:27:34-07:00","id":938234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBoyDante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/938071-several-rules-questions-humanity-defence-to-disciplines-defending-others-safe-house?p=938218#post938218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise of the argument is you have no other choice, your too far away to run Inbetween, no thrown weapons near by, tried to shout but he ignored you, only have celerity and already used your vitae this turn only have a gun in hand and if you don't act now he will be stabbed. You aim for the arm to get him to stop but it severs an artery and he bleeds out.<br /> <br /> And it's about if that is a low breaking point I wouldn't see it personally as a low breaking point for my humanity I would be praised a hero and feel good that I saved someone. Humanity wise it may still haunt me but I don't think it should be a 2 breaking point is what I'm saying. I think it should be lowest 4 but would place it at 5 self defence with no other option still bad but not as bad as premeditated/passioned killing which we see as crimes of passion like you come home your wife's cheating and you snap and kill her. I still see it as a breaking point but just don't think it should be on the same level as premeditated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose pretty much said put it where it feels right. You have had several examples, most of us think it's somewhere between 1-7. <br /> <br /> I personally dont think self-defense should be where premeditated murder is, but if you shifted into an animal and just left this person in 100 pieces all over the place.. maybe it should be. But what everyone seems to agree on... is that it is how it is done and that depends on the situation. <br /> <br /> @MCN yes stabbing is bashing ( but again situational ) what if your vampire has 6 health and they are stabbing you for 4 per turn. even then you wont last very long...But you're right. most scenarios you can get out of without killing someone. that would be a more rarer case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:11:03-07:00","id":938263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBoyDante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/938071-several-rules-questions-humanity-defence-to-disciplines-defending-others-safe-house?p=938180#post938180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the humanity point as 2 is premeditated your saying that someone who thinks you know what I'm going to kill this pregnant woman because she won't give me her purse is the same as there's a murderer he just killed one person he's about to stab a child he is bringing down the knife you have a second to react so as you have a gun in hand you shoot him it is a lucky shot (lots of open rolls) and manages to kill him is the same? I tell you I would feel a lot worse killing a pregnant woman to get her purse than shooting a murderer who was about to kill a child because I had no other choice. I would still feel bad I killed him but would seek solace in the fact I had no choice and he was about to kill a child.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's quote the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The listed breaking points are examples only. Add breaking points at Storyteller discretion, or shift these up or down to fit the situation. Typically, the more personal the event is, the lower level a breaking</span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\"> point it should be. If something is significantly distanced from the character, or she had no way to prevent it, it should be a Humanity level higher. </span> </div> </div> </div>Trying to save a child is a very human and humane act so you can bump the breaking point up a bit.<br /> <br /> Edit: ninja'd<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","user":"Ophion","date":".  aaand I didn't refresh the page. D'oh. 07-27-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:30:15-07:00","id":938273,"title":"","content":"1 - I'd put killing in self-defense at Humanity 3, same as impassioned killing. The need to defend yourself is the thing flaring your passion.<br /> <br /> 2 - The sidebar about eye-contact for the purposes of Dominate says the victim needs to see the vampire's eyes. You don't need to be locking eyes with the vampire, you just need to be able to see their eyes. So unless you're looking at the floor or something, no, you can't avoid what constitutes eye-contact for the purposes of Dominate. And good luck getting through (un)life never looking at anything but your feet.<br /> <br /> 3 - I would allow the bodyguard to voluntarily act as a human shield (grants the person they're protecting Cover, with durability equal to Stamina + Armor, and takes all the damage from the attack).<br /> <br /> 4 - The Safe Place rules are intentionally abstract. The fact that you need to go to the trouble of disabling security cameras, drugging guard dogs, etc. is represented by the dice penalty to your roll to break in. Hacking Software and drugged meat and such could maybe grant an equipment bonus to the roll to break in, but it's not going to allow you to bypass the roll entirely. Personally, I would probably not allow fire-based traps on a Safe Place because of the way fire works. The damage is dependent on the size and intensity of the fire, and continues to deal that much damage every turn that the victim is in the affected area. The intent of the trap damage from Safe Place is clearly a single one-and-done amount of damage, and fire just doesn't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-27-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:50:32-07:00","id":938282,"title":"","content":"Yea I posted before I saw Roses post and me and my friend take anything by Rose as law obviously so yea I'm happy. And thanks for commenting, normally we take ideas from here but only definitively set rules if Rose comments so thank you. Yea from what I'm getting people still think it's low humanity but have it where it feels right.<br /> <br /> Thank you all for you help I really appreciate it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12176-theboydante","name":"TheBoyDante","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T14:15:34-07:00","id":938324,"title":"","content":"@4: I wouldn\u00b4t try to break in. .... I would rather convince Homeland Security or a very influential police man, that the person who lives there (the target) is a terrorist or a very dangerous cult leader. <br /> <br /> One could achive this e.g. by using dominate or majesty or blood bonds on influential people in the state executive system ... The bigger your security efforts, the more plausible a terrorist / cult leader story sounds ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11546-christoph","name":"Christoph+","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T14:53:44-07:00","id":938342,"title":"","content":"If your player is really insistent about not making eye contact just hammer a huge penalty on all his social rolls. Speeches are far less compelling when the speaker is staring at the floor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T15:24:52-07:00","id":938378,"title":"","content":"I would suggest offering a middle ground by agreeing that's a cool idea that definitely makes their character unique, and would:<br /> 1.) Hammer out a Condition for that<br /> 2.) Suggest going full Ordo and turning that paranoia into obsession of getting your eyes out because they are unsafe, so unsafe, they are gates to your soul, and they are open by default, you need to close them, CLOSE THEM!<br /> <br /> I mean, how many of your plot points hinge on that particular player getting Dominated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T16:37:58-07:00","id":938426,"title":"","content":"I had a vampire who was against a Ventrue Elder that liked Dominate a lot. He had acute senses, sunglasses with nailpolish on the inside lenses, and a tape recorder on him at all times when meeting. The Ventrue was routinely pissed at my character figuring ways around dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T17:09:07-07:00","id":938437,"title":"","content":"I think if the player just absolutely doesn't want to be Dominated, the easiest thing to do is to agree that the story won't go there. Strategies against the Discipline and finding ways to eke out modifiers ultimately preserve the chance of failure. Playing a tricky character can be fun, but if the player feels like they have to be constantly on the defensive to avoid some particular thing... it's easiest to just take that thing off the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:11:24-07:00","id":939069,"title":"","content":"My take on self defense is it depends.<br /> <br /> Did you mean to just knock them unconscious and hit a bit to hard? That's accidental. That being said, its hard to say that you were just trying to hurt someone with a gun.<br /> Did you get to emotional, went overboard and were scared or angry? That's impassioned. Killing someone in frenzy is probably here as well.<br /> Did the street punk pull a knife on you and you decided you would just end them there to get the rest of his gang in line? That's premeditated.<br /> <br /> In my mind, the fact that you have a reason is not a non factor. Characters (and people too) always have a reason for why they do something, good or bad.<br /> <br /> They have always suggested that you insert your own take on things. Do you want high adventure like &quot;Underworld&quot; or more of a morality tale like &quot;Near Dark&quot; or &quot;Byzantium&quot;? Turn the dials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:25:56-07:00","id":941252,"title":"","content":"I used Protean to blind my character and have sonar vision in its stead. It's a viable strategy if your player is interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T11:24:25-07:00","id":941281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/938071-several-rules-questions-humanity-defence-to-disciplines-defending-others-safe-house?p=938217#post938217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I'd let the bodyguard add one Attribute or Skill to the defended character's Defense. Depending on the context, this might be Stamina (I'm protecting you with the sheer bulk of my body), Weaponry (I'm blocking attacks on you using a tool or weapon), Dexterity (I jump between you and your attacker with lightning speed), or even Resolve (I resist my fear of fire to stand between you and the torch-wielding hunter).<br /> <br /> If that pushes Defense too high for your taste, consider something like substituting the bodyguard's appropriate stat for the defended character's Athletics in calculating Defense.<br /> <br /> A character should not be able to benefit from a bodyguard physically blocking attacks while also making attacks themselves. Unless maybe they have a cool new description for how they do it, in which case go to town. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. Another way to do it would be to treat it kind of like teamwork. The bodyguard makes an appropriate roll (let's say strength+brawl) as their action and the successes are defense bonus. If you want to make it more effective, have it be deduced from the attacker's successes, but I think the first one is decent enough.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't worry about it making the defense too high. I mean, attacking someone while being blocked by someone else is really really hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T14:01:01-07:00","id":941390,"title":"","content":"Actually after reading some of the books where they talk about avoiding eye contact, I was under the impression that it<i> was</i> generally how things were done. Of course if you're concentrating on avoiding someones eyes in combat, then your focus is then split between that and the actual combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T03:56:28-07:00","id":941815,"title":"","content":"The eye contact thing is a funny point. If a player insists that they never look anyone in the eyes, they should definitely have penalties. You can't make a conscious effort to avoid eye contact with everyone and not be inconvenienced, so you should probably suffer penalties for pretty much every task as long as someone else is around. I also don't think it's as simple as not looking someone directly in the eye. Even having someone's eyes in your field of vision is dangerous because you don't control all your eye movements when you're looking around. There's a good chance that, if you can see a person's face, you're going to lock eyes with them even for a split second accidentally. That would be crippling during a fight (making eye contact at a time like that for the dominate use wouldn't necessarily be easy, but not as much as avoiding all eye contact) because unless you're in very close quarter or in a grapple, that means you're not looking at a whole portion of your opponent.<br /> <br /> Anyway, one of my players has a character that really really hates anything resembling mind control (blood bonds, and most mental disciplines). We we did a few times was that if he would look at me in the eyes, I would roll dominate. Usually, it didn't take long before I got to make my roll. The first time, he knew he was facing a ventrue and they started fighting (he was way better than the ventrue) until he stabbed him for pretty big damage. Then, he looked at me and I had the ventrue dominate him. Then, the second time he wasn't aware of all the vampire could do. The vampire waited for the party outside a room, started gloating, then called the PC's name and I looked at him the eyes. Took him a second to understand and turn his head away, but that was it.<br /> <br /> It's hard not looking people in the eye, you go against your basic instincts and habits doing so. That reminds me of a 1st Ed Ordo Dracul series of three merits. The third one, Mind of the Inscrutable Hydra allowed the vampire to go into a state of mind where all mental disciplines would have -2 penalties to affect them (or a +3 bonus for resistance roll), but since it was a conscious mental defense mechanism, it also imposed a -2 penalty on all of the vampire's Intelligence-base rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:43:23-07:00","id":941936,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the character is going to have major trust issues, would be great to take advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}